      },
      {
        "id": "E7",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "A: At the most basic level, our job is to convert designs into the physical world.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/ai-infrastructure-supply-chain/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-16T20:00:37.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-16T20:22:52.584Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E8",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Our design team creates a blueprint, and our job is to transition it into a reliable, high-performance supply chain.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/ai-infrastructure-supply-chain/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-16T20:00:37.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-16T20:22:52.584Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E9",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "In this large cable cartridge, there are 1,500 small cable legs.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/ai-infrastructure-supply-chain/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-16T20:00:37.000Z",
